From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:08:18 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] rocket: v15 order of the reset put, for an A/B against v16
 (TEST ONLY)

Drop the job's runtime PM reference inside job_lock before the IOMMU
detach and the core reset, as v15's 4/15 did. Fork CI only.

Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c | 10 +++-------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
index 5fbb94875658..7ee13be5cb19 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -391,8 +391,6 @@ static void rocket_job_handle_irq(struct rocket_core *core)
 static void
 rocket_reset(struct rocket_core *core, struct drm_sched_job *bad)
 {
-	bool put_job_ref;
-
 	if (!atomic_read(&core->reset.pending))
 		return;
 
@@ -411,10 +409,11 @@ rocket_reset(struct rocket_core *core, struct drm_sched_job *bad)
 	/*
 	 * Remaining interrupts have been handled, but we might still have
 	 * stuck jobs. Let's make sure the PM counters stay balanced by
-	 * dropping the job's reference once the core has been reset.
+	 * dropping the job's reference.
 	 */
 	scoped_guard(mutex, &core->job_lock) {
-		put_job_ref = core->in_flight_job;
+		if (core->in_flight_job)
+			pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(core->dev);
 
 		iommu_detach_group(NULL, core->iommu_group);
 
@@ -424,9 +423,6 @@ rocket_reset(struct rocket_core *core, struct drm_sched_job *bad)
 	/* Proceed with reset now. */
 	rocket_core_reset(core);
 
-	if (put_job_ref)
-		pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(core->dev);
-
 	/* NPU has been reset, we can clear the reset pending bit. */
 	atomic_set(&core->reset.pending, 0);
 
-- 
